  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="c812-d3e4-8cf6-25da" name="Return of the Bulgars (Vlad the Impaler) - List Notes" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF THE BULGARS (Vlad the Impaler, pp.75-76): Bulgar armies of the late 13th and 14th centuries (1280-1396). Allies from other lists are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Return of the Bulgars]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  ARMIES OF THE BULGARS (1280-1396). Characters up to 25%; Cavalry at least 50% (the number of Pronija Retainer units may not be greater than the number of Provincial Pronija units; must take 1+ unit of Cuman Settler/Bulgar Horse Archers for every 1,000 pts); Infantry up to 25% (0-1 Mangonel may be taken for every 1,000 pts); Allies up to 25%; additionally, Bulgars may select allies from Serbia (may not take Artillery), Byzantium (may not take Kavallarioi or Artillery) and Walachia (Small Host - may not take Artillery) (documented only). All allies are subject to the Allies and Mercenaries rule.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
